  "cover_text": "Mahatma Gandhi1 once said, “The world provides enough for the birds and no for the bees; the world provides enough for the wine in bottles and no for the food in tummies; the world supplies enough for us to eat and plenty for others, but no for them to eat.” The individuals involved in mass food aid misinterpret Gandhi’s statement, which he meant as critical, as a call for Jesus-like bloodshed. Gandhi insisted, however, that he hoped to inspire strength to those who are under criminal oppression, instead of just impose a gap-fill in the performance of action to appease the feeling of superiority within the agents",
